INT. FLOODED PARKING GARAGE - LEVEL B3 - NIGHT

Ankle-deep water. A Buick idles with its trunk open, stuffed with cash bags.

RENATA VOSS (40s, crew boss, rain slicker) faces four others. JUNIOR MBEKI (20s, driver) fiddles with a flashlight. OLD TOMASZ (60s, safecracker, trembling hands). WREN (20s, lookout, hoodie). CALLOWAY (30s, inside man, bank lanyard).

RENATA
Everybody listen. Count is short by two bags.

Nobody moves.

CALLOWAY
(to Renata)
You counted wrong.

RENATA
I counted twice.

OLD TOMASZ
(muttering)
Three bags I carried. Three. I carried three.

JUNIOR
Somebody took them. That's what short means.

Calloway lunges at Junior. They crash into the Buick, water spraying. Wren pulls them apart.

WREN
Enough! Headlights, up the ramp!

Everyone freezes. Light washes the wall. Then it passes.

RENATA
(to herself)
Breathe, Renata.

WREN
It's gone. Okay. It's gone.

A bag splashes in the water by Tomasz's feet. He stares at it. They all stare at him.

The group scatters. Tires skid. The Buick lurches away, leaving Tomasz alone, whispering to himself.
